  "mathematical_scope": "The arguments use the geometric and coefficient hypotheses stated in each lesson. Appendices BZ–CB prove the geometric fibre comparison (BY.26) for bounded constructible complexes over a finite coefficient field of characteristic different from that of the finite or algebraically closed ground field; a finite extension of a finite ground field is allowed. Together with BO–BY, this gives the integral and rational realization statements under their stated coefficient hypotheses. The general course proofs remain incomplete: other canonical-appendix inputs and their transitive prerequisites, arbitrary-trait nearby cycles, several later comparison theorems and the general stack and Riemann–Hilbert statements require further proofs."
